<p>From Fort Lewis, Ervin and several other soldiers were sent to Officer Candidate School in Fort Sill, OK (the site of the principal artillery araining school) After Ervin was commissioned 2nd lieutenant, he was reassigned to Camp Roberts, CA to train soldiers.While at Camp Roberts, Ervin met Leona Kelley. They were married on September 1, 1943. Ervin was later reassigned and dispatched to study at Officers' Training School. Two weeks after their son Steven was born June 26, 1944, Ervin was deployed to the Pacific Theater of War. Promoted to 1st lieutenant, he was assigned battery commander of the 363rd Field Artillery 96th Division. The unit was involved in the invasions of Leyte, Phillipine Islands and Okinawa. Leona and Ervin Rybnicek</p>

